course: dictionary
lesson: 3576
title: Fever: more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fever is when your body is hotter than normal because it is fighting germs. «A fever is when the body raises its temperature to fight infection» tells you the fever is a sign that your body is working hard.
explain: Fever has a second meaning too. Football fever is a state of great excitement, when everyone is buzzing about the match. The same word can mean something in your body or something in a crowd, so use the context to decide. «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness» is about illness, because of the aching, the shivers and the tiredness.
explain: Be careful with hay fever. It has fever in its name, but it is an allergy, not a real fever. «Antihistamine tablets, nasal sprays or eye drops help hay fever, and you cannot catch it from someone else.» The clue is that you cannot catch it.
fact: Fever means your body temperature is higher than normal because you are ill.
fact: Normal body temperature is about 37 °C (98.6 °F), and a fever is above about 38 °C (100.4 °F).
fact: A fever is the body fighting germs, so rest and drink plenty of water.
fact: «Fever pitch» and «football fever» mean great excitement.
fact: Hay fever is an allergy, not a real fever, and you cannot catch it from someone else.
exercise: «Flu comes on suddenly with high fever, aching muscles, headache, shivers and great tiredness.» What does fever mean here? | *A body temperature higher than normal because you are ill | A sore, aching leg | Great excitement, like football fever | A thermometer for measuring the sun
exercise: The fans had football fever before the final. What does fever mean in this sentence? | A cold, wet day | A high temperature from germs | *Great excitement | Being sick in bed
exercise: «Rest, drink plenty, and tell an adult if you have a fever.» What should you do if you have a fever? | *Rest, drink plenty and tell an adult | Run around to sweat it out | Stay quiet and say nothing
test: What is hay fever? | Cabin fever from staying indoors | *An allergy, not a real fever | A very high temperature from a germ
test: What is a fever above about 38 °C? | A normal body temperature of 37 °C | A reading on a map | A cold drink | *A temperature higher than normal
exam: Which phrase means restless from staying indoors too long? | Fever pitch | *Cabin fever | Hay fever | Football fever
